  "question": {
    "text": "<p>From the given list, the number of compounds with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo> </mo></math>oxidation state of Sulphur</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>SOCl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>SF</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>BaSO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo> </mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>7</mn></msub></math></p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The total number of electrons that an atom either gains or loses in order to form a chemical bond with another atom is known as the Oxidation Number.</p><p>In <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math></p><p> Let the oxidation number of S be x.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo> </mo><mo>+</mo><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo> </mo><mo>+</mo><mo> </mo><mn>3</mn><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mo> </mo><mo>=</mo><mo> </mo><mn>0</mn><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo> </mo><mo>=</mo><mo> </mo><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></math> </p><p>Similarly the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo> </mo></math>oxidation state of sulphur is shown by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>SOCl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo> </mo><mi>and</mi><mo> </mo><msub><mi>SF</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnlines=\"solid\" frame=\"solid\" rowlines=\"solid\"><mtr><mtd><mtext> Compounds </mtext></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>SOCl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>SF</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>BaSO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo> </mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>7</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mtext> O.S.of Sulphur: </mtext></mtd><mtd><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p>"
  }
